exports[`roleAssignmentRequest follows the connectivity choice (C1) > is unchanged for full connectivity (existing) 1`] = `
"Change request: assign Azure RBAC roles for Cribl SOC Toolkit (setup path: existing)

Requesting application: Cribl SOC Toolkit
Service principal (client id): 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Tenant id: 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

What is requested
-----------------
Assign the following roles to the service principal for Cribl SOC Toolkit (client id: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111):
- Reader at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
- Monitoring Contributor at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab
- Log Analytics Contributor at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab
- Microsoft Sentinel Contributor at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab  [feature]
- RBAC Administrator at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab  [feature]
    Condition: Constrain roles and principal types: only Monitoring Metrics Publisher, only to service principals.
- Azure Event Hubs Data Owner at the Event Hub namespace that holds the rule  [feature]
- Security Admin at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab (the default; the role is needed on whichever resource group you deploy CriblDefenderExport into in the Defender section)  [feature]

[feature] roles each unlock one named capability and can be refused on
their own; the untagged roles are what this setup path needs to work at all.

Justification
-------------
- Reader (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333): Discover subscriptions, resource groups, workspaces, and existing DCRs before deploying.
- Monitoring Contributor (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Create and update Data Collection Rules in the workspace resource group.
- Log Analytics Contributor (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Create custom Log Analytics tables and configure the workspace for ingestion.
- Microsoft Sentinel Contributor (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Installing analytic rules and workbooks, and onboarding a workspace to Sentinel, WRITE Microsoft.SecurityInsights resources. Log Analytics Contributor grants read across the subscription but no Microsoft.SecurityInsights write, so without this role the install fails on the first rule.
- RBAC Administrator (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Data only flows through a Data Collection Rule if the sending identity holds Monitoring Metrics Publisher ON THAT RULE, and creating a role assignment is itself a privileged action that Contributor does not include. Attach the condition below so this grant cannot be used to assign anything else.
- Azure Event Hubs Data Owner (the Event Hub namespace that holds the rule): Creating the Cribl Event Hub source with the listKeys credential, and deploying the Defender continuous export, read the connection string of a namespace shared access rule (POST .../authorizationRules/{rule}/listKeys). That is an /action, which Reader does not grant: Reader passes every Event Hub rule check in Validate while listKeys still returns 403. A custom role with only authorizationRules/listKeys/action and authorizationRules/read on the namespace is narrower still.
- Security Admin (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab (the default; the role is needed on whichever resource group you deploy CriblDefenderExport into in the Defender section)): The export is a Microsoft.Security/automations resource (CriblDefenderExport) the app creates in the resource group chosen in the Defender section; creating it needs automations/write, which neither Reader nor the Monitoring and Log Analytics roles include.

Specifics
---------
Service principal (client id): 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Tenant id:                     22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Setup path:                    existing
Subscription:                  33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
Resource group:                rg-soc-lab

Why (deploy and ingestion flows)
--------------------------------
\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart LR
app["Cribl SOC Toolkit (Cribl app)"]
arm["Azure Resource Manager - subscription 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"]
dcr["DCR + custom table - resource group rg-soc-lab - workspace law-soc-lab"]
app -->|deploy ARM template| arm
arm -->|create DCR + table| dcr
\`\`\`

\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart LR
diag["Azure diagnostic settings - subscription 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"]
eh["Event Hub"]
cribl["Cribl Stream - reduce / normalize"]
sentinel["Microsoft Sentinel - workspace law-soc-lab - resource group rg-soc-lab"]
diag -->|stream events| eh
eh -->|pull events| cribl
cribl -->|Logs Ingestion API via DCR| sentinel
\`\`\`"
`;

exports[`roleAssignmentRequest follows the connectivity choice (C1) > is unchanged for full connectivity (lab-byo-rg) 1`] = `
"Change request: assign Azure RBAC roles for Cribl SOC Toolkit (setup path: lab-byo-rg)

Requesting application: Cribl SOC Toolkit
Service principal (client id): 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Tenant id: 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

What is requested
-----------------
Assign the following roles to the service principal for Cribl SOC Toolkit (client id: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111):
- Contributor at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab
- RBAC Administrator at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab
    Condition: Constrain roles and principal types: only Contributor and Monitoring Metrics Publisher, only to service principals.
- Azure Event Hubs Data Owner at the Event Hub namespace that holds the rule  [feature]
- Security Reader at /subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333  [feature]

[feature] roles each unlock one named capability and can be refused on
their own; the untagged roles are what this setup path needs to work at all.

Justification
-------------
- Contributor (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Deploy the lab workspace, DCRs, and tables into the pre-created lab resource group. The grant reaches nothing outside it: the Event Grid provider registration (subscription) and the regional Network Watcher (NetworkWatcherRG) need rights there, or an admin who registers the provider and creates the watcher first.
- RBAC Administrator (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/resourceGroups/rg-soc-lab): Assign the lab TTL self-destruct identity its delete role on the lab resource group at deploy time.
- Azure Event Hubs Data Owner (the Event Hub namespace that holds the rule): Creating the Cribl Event Hub source with the listKeys credential, and deploying the Defender continuous export, read the connection string of a namespace shared access rule (POST .../authorizationRules/{rule}/listKeys). That is an /action, which Reader does not grant: Reader passes every Event Hub rule check in Validate while listKeys still returns 403. A custom role with only authorizationRules/listKeys/action and authorizationRules/read on the namespace is narrower still.
- Security Reader (/subscriptions/33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333): Before deploying the export the app reads which Defender plans are on (pricings/read) and lists the subscription's continuous exports (automations/read) so it never creates a duplicate.

Specifics
---------
Service principal (client id): 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Tenant id:                     22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Setup path:                    lab-byo-rg
Subscription:                  33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333
Resource group:                rg-soc-lab

Why (deploy and ingestion flows)
--------------------------------
\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart LR
app["Cribl SOC Toolkit (Cribl app)"]
arm["Azure Resource Manager - subscription 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"]
dcr["DCR + custom table - resource group rg-soc-lab - workspace law-soc-lab"]
app -->|deploy ARM template| arm
arm -->|create DCR + table| dcr
\`\`\`

\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart LR
diag["Azure diagnostic settings - subscription 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333"]
eh["Event Hub"]
cribl["Cribl Stream - reduce / normalize"]
sentinel["Microsoft Sentinel - workspace law-soc-lab - resource group rg-soc-lab"]
diag -->|stream events| eh
eh -->|pull events| cribl
cribl -->|Logs Ingestion API via DCR| sentinel
\`\`\`"
`;

